From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] A lesson leaves a draft and follow-ups that a person
 approves

What a finished online lesson leaves behind, and who may act on it:
lesson_metrics, lesson_feedback (the teacher's own coaching), lesson_recordings
(readable by the household only while the recording consent is in force),
lesson_followups and ai_usage, all written by worker_store_lesson_results
(service role, quiet for a lesson older than a day; a concern files a task in
the room's pool at once, a retry proposes nothing twice).

approve_followup keeps every family-facing word a person's: a teacher's yes
only marks the row approved and pushes the room's in-charges; an in-charge
or admin sends the message as themselves through start_family_direct and
messages, writes the standing note through add_student_note, or files the
task, and the row is done with the id written back. dismiss_followup says no.

Two notify_push pairs join the list, so the three places that hold it
(the migrations, DEPLOYMENT.md, send-push's header) say twenty-eight, and
the schedule check now expects the fourteenth cron job.

